We denote vectors by ⃗ vand use capital letters to refer to
matrices. For example, A∈En×mis a matrix of size n×m
with elements belonging to a set of permissible values, E.
Specifically, if E={0,1}(resp. E={−1,0,1}), then
A∈En×mis denoted as a binary (resp. ternary ) matrix.
