6. Conclusion
This paper presented algorithms that significantly improve
inference time and memory efficiency for quantized neu-
ral networks (like LLMs) with binary and ternary weights.
By preprocessing weight matrices to create indices, our
approach reduces storage complexity for maintaining the
model weights by a logarithmic factor. It enhances inference
efficiency, achieving a time complexity of O(n2
logn).
Furthermore, our experiment results across various settings
demonstrated the practical advantages of our methods, with
observed reductions in inference time of up to 29x and
memory usage of up to 6x.
