To optimize the runtime of the previously discussed CPU
implementation on the GPU, we parallelized the vector-
matrix multiplication. Using the segmentation matrix M,
the multiplication was parallelized along its second dimen-
sion, corresponding to k(see Section 4.2.2). To achieve this,
we first expanded the input vector to a size ktimes larger:
1 input_expanded = input .unsqueeze(1).
expand(-1, k, -1)
